# The descending `p`-central series and its refinement

This file formalizes Definition 3 of A. Schmidt and K. Wingberg, *Šafarevič's theorem on
solvable groups as Galois groups* (arXiv:math/9809211):

* the descending `p`-central series of a group `P`,
  `P₁ = P`, `P_{i+1} = (P_i)^p [P_i, P]`;
* the descending central series `P₁ = P`, `P_{i+1} = [P_i, P]` (the special case `p = 1`
  of the `p`-central series up to the generated powers; we only record the `p`-central
  series here);
* the refinement `P_{(i,j)} = (P_i ∩ P_j) P_{i+1}`, `i, j ≥ 1`, ordered lexicographically,
  with `τ + 1 = (i, j+1)` for `i > j` and `τ + 1 = (i+1, 1)` for `τ = (i, i)`.

## Indexing conventions

The paper's series starts at `P₁ = P`.  We index by `ℕ` starting at `0`, so that
`pCentralSeries p P 0 = ⊤` and `pCentralSeries p P (n+1) = pCentralStep p (pCentralSeries p P n)`.
Thus **`pCentralSeries p P n` is the paper's `P_{n+1}`**.

The refinement `pCentralRefined p P i j` is indexed by the paper's indices `i, j ≥ 1`, i.e.
`pCentralRefined p P i j = (P_i ∩ P_j) P_{i+1}`.

## Main results

* `Work.Shrinking.pCentralSeries_le_succ`, `Work.Shrinking.pCentralSeries_antitone` : the
  series is descending.
* `Work.Shrinking.pCentralSeries_normal`, `Work.Shrinking.pCentralSeries_characteristic` :
  every term is normal, indeed characteristic.
* `Work.Shrinking.pow_mem_pCentralSeries_succ`, `Work.Shrinking.commutator_le_pCentralSeries_succ` :
  the defining properties of the next term.
* `Work.Shrinking.pCentralRefined_one`, `Work.Shrinking.pCentralRefined_eq_succ` : the
  refinement has the properties `P_{(i,1)} = P_i` and `P_{(i,j)} = P_{i+1}` for `j > i`.
-/

import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.Shrinking.Basic
-- PORT435-BEGIN (v4.35 isDefEq respectTransparency compat)
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false
-- PORT435-END

namespace Work.Shrinking

universe u

/-! ## The series -/

section Defs

variable {P : Type*} [Group P]

/-- The subgroup generated by the `p`-th powers of the elements of `H`: the paper's `H^p`. -/
def powSubgroup (p : ℕ) (H : Subgroup P) : Subgroup P :=
  Subgroup.closure ((fun x : P => x ^ p) '' (H : Set P))

/-- The next term of the descending `p`-central series of a subgroup: `H^p [H, P]`. -/
def pCentralStep (p : ℕ) (H : Subgroup P) : Subgroup P :=
  powSubgroup p H ⊔ ⁅H, ⊤⁆

/-- The descending `p`-central series of a group `P` (Definition 3 of Schmidt–Wingberg):
`pCentralSeries p P 0 = ⊤` and `pCentralSeries p P (n+1) = (pCentralSeries p P n)^p [pCentralSeries p P n, P]`.
So `pCentralSeries p P n` is the paper's `P_{n+1}`. -/
def pCentralSeries (p : ℕ) (P : Type*) [Group P] : ℕ → Subgroup P
  | 0 => ⊤
  | n + 1 => pCentralStep p (pCentralSeries p P n)

/-- The refinement `P_{(i,j)} = (P_i ∩ P_j) P_{i+1}` of the descending `p`-central series
(Definition 3 of Schmidt–Wingberg), indexed as in the paper (`i, j ≥ 1`). -/
def pCentralRefined (p : ℕ) (P : Type*) [Group P] (i j : ℕ) : Subgroup P :=
  (pCentralSeries p P (i - 1) ⊓ pCentralSeries p P (j - 1)) ⊔ pCentralSeries p P i

@[simp]
theorem pCentralSeries_zero (p : ℕ) (P : Type*) [Group P] : pCentralSeries p P 0 = ⊤ := rfl

theorem pCentralSeries_succ (p : ℕ) (P : Type*) [Group P] (n : ℕ) :
    pCentralSeries p P (n + 1) = pCentralStep p (pCentralSeries p P n) := rfl

/-- `H^p ≤ H` for a subgroup `H`. -/
theorem powSubgroup_le (p : ℕ) (H : Subgroup P) : powSubgroup p H ≤ H := by
  unfold powSubgroup
  rw [Subgroup.closure_le]
  rintro x ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
  exact H.pow_mem hy p

/-- `[H, P] ≤ H` for a normal subgroup `H`. -/
theorem commutator_le_self_of_normal (H : Subgroup P) [H.Normal] : ⁅H, ⊤⁆ ≤ H :=
  Subgroup.commutator_le_left H ⊤

end Defs

end Work.Shrinking
